From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8450: enable the parents of SM8475's UFS AXI
 clock while switching

SM8475's UFS AXI clock reaches its turbo rates from GPLL2. ufshcd sets
the rate at probe before it enables the clock, so GPLL2 is not running
when the RCG switches to it, and the update times out:
"gcc_ufs_phy_axi_clk_src: rcg didn't update its configuration". Keep
both parents on across the switch, as SM8150 and SM8250 do for their
SDCC2 clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8450.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8450.c
@@ -1076,7 +1076,7 @@
 	.name = "gcc_ufs_phy_axi_clk_src",
 	.parent_data = sm8475_gcc_parent_data_3,
 	.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(sm8475_gcc_parent_map_3),
-	.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+	.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
 	.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
 };
 
